WEBVTT

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:09.820
I'm sick and tired of hiding!

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:15.690
Sessai-sensei, when do I 
get to fight Nobunaga?

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.120
It's not time yet, Yoshimoto-sama.

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:22.420
I'm tired of hearing that!

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:24.460
When will it be time?

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:27.460
You'll know when the time comes.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:30.060
And I'm tired of hearing that, too!

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:34.670
You once felt for yourself 
how terrifying she can be.

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:38.300
That's true, but...

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:40.540
Pathetic!

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.470
You're pathetic, Imagawa Yoshimoto!

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:45.260
Did you think you could

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:49.970
fight the Little Devil 
King with power like that?

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:54.080
Are you okay with challenging 
Nobunaga before

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:56.320
you're ready, and losing again?

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:01.740
I should be much stronger 
than I was back then, too!

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:05.750
And Nobunaga may not 
be who she was, either.

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:08.380
Well...

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:11.150
No, she may actually be training

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:13.260
and becoming much stronger.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:08.590
Quiet.

00:03:09.190 --> 00:03:10.200
Kotaro?

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:13.170
How have things been going 
since then, Kotaro?

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:14.770
Going?

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:15.840
Going with what?

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:21.680
I gave you the mission of 
distracting Yoshimoto-sama.

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:23.750
It's fine, then.

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:26.380
She loves sweets.

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:28.320
So I bought a bunch of 
Okinawan black sugar

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:29.560
on the shopping channel!

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:31.710
I see.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:37.030
Did you say the shopping 
channel, Kotaro?

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:38.940
What, Sessai-sama?

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:40.740
You don't know the shopping channel?

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:42.360
Everyone knows it in this world.

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:50.370
<b>1.) A ninja must be stealthy.
2.) A ninja must be deceptive.
3.) A ninja must be flexible.</b>

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:45.600
I do, that's why I'm asking.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:49.770
You do know this is a secret base, right?

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:55.220
Why are you getting

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:59.270
a package shipped to our secret base?!

00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:01.490
What do you think will happen if Nobunaga

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:04.470
finds this place?

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:06.660
I-It'll be fine!

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:11.370
I kept the address a secret!

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:10.470
Take this! And this!

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:13.350
I see.

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:17.210
So nobody will find out 
about this base, then.

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:22.350
But then the package won't get here!

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:24.900
So there's no point!

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:27.950
I didn't think of that!

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:34.490
However, it was my mistake 
to expect too much

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:37.840
out of your tiny brain and 
give you a vague order.

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:38.980
That's right.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:39.750
Your mistake.

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:43.020
Very well.

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:48.670
This is a list of sweets I 
prepared for this eventuality.

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:56.100
<b>Cheese zuccotto from Gateau Puniue
Striped Roll from Monchuchu
Tiramisu from Fortefruite
Imo-youkan from Imosenyamasen</b>

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:54.610
You will go buy them. Okay, Kotaro?

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:56.100
Yes...

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:02.400
Back!

00:05:04.210 --> 00:05:06.870
Yoshimoto-sama, I bought you a

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:08.730
cheese zuccotto from Gateau Puniue!

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:14.830
It's great.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:16.620
Is it?

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:22.220
Yoshimoto-sama!

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:24.280
A striped roll from Monchuchu!

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:28.470
This is good, too.

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:30.600
Yoshimoto-sama,

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:33.600
Here's tiramisu from Fortefruite.

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:35.350
Buono!

00:05:36.010 --> 00:05:38.560
Yoshimoto-sama,

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:43.260
I bought some imo-youkan 
from Imosenyamasen.

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:46.170
Bonissimo!

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:49.660
I think I like Japanese candies more.

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:54.540
Sessai-sama, even a ninja 
doesn't have enough

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:58.370
energy to go all around 
Japan buying things.

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:03.750
And it's clearly having an adverse 
effect on Yoshimoto-sama, too.

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:07.260
<i>I can't believe you!</i>

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:09.260
<i>What are you thinking?</i>

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:12.260
<i>Regarding that...</i>

00:06:15.070 --> 00:06:17.990
<i>It's a kappa!</i>

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:22.430
<i>But it's on the other side of 
the river, so I can't go see it!</i>

00:06:22.430 --> 00:06:24.030
<i>It ran away!</i>

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:25.780
<i>Follow it!</i>

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:29.810
It seems I should solve this in a manner

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:32.280
that's better for her health.

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:40.430
One, two, three!

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:43.340
Well, Yoshimoto-sama?

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:46.120
Isn't outdoor air great?

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:46.840
Right?

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:52.340
The air's fine, but the 
bugs are unpleasant.

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:56.910
I didn't know there were places 
like this in this world!

00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:59.350
I feel like I'm home.

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:02.180
Kotaro, did you grow up

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:03.730
in the middle of nowhere like this?

00:07:04.010 --> 00:07:06.040
That's a secret!

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:10.200
That's your personality, isn't it?

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:17.050
Once you get out here, 
the river's clean and clear!

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:20.370
There are fish, too, Yoshimoto-sama!

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:23.540
Seems so.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:27.990
A waterfall!

00:07:27.990 --> 00:07:30.050
There's a waterfall, Yoshimoto-sama!

00:07:31.730 --> 00:07:34.610
It's huge.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:41.630
Hey, isn't that Sou'un 
under that waterfall?

00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:43.230
You're right.

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:45.640
She said she was going to train.

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:47.240
Is this where she came?

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:51.730
Hey, stupid Sou'un!

00:07:51.730 --> 00:07:54.740
Come say hi to Yoshimoto-sama!

00:07:57.920 --> 00:08:00.700
What, she's ignoring us?

00:08:06.870 --> 00:08:09.530
Well, the rice is done.

00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:11.590
What about the rest?

00:08:12.350 --> 00:08:13.880
We source locally.

00:08:14.910 --> 00:08:16.890
Source locally?

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:33.620
Ashigara Style Giacobinids Fishing!

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:43.910
So you lure in the carp with bread,

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:48.290
then put a piece on a hook 
and throw it in there.

00:09:06.590 --> 00:09:10.270
It looks like anybody could do that.

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:11.530
That's right.

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:13.420
Anybody can catch carp.

00:09:13.420 --> 00:09:15.400
They're dumb.

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:16.970
So any idiot could catch them.

00:09:16.970 --> 00:09:18.780
Even you could do it, Yoshimoto-sama!

00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:21.410
Now see here...

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:26.420
So I just throw this 
where the carp are, right?

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:28.860
Easy!

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:35.570
I think I went a tad far.

00:09:35.570 --> 00:09:36.820
A tad?

00:09:36.820 --> 00:09:38.730
Just a tad!

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:51.020
Are you okay, Yoshimoto-sama?

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:58.820
Fishing is far more fun than 
I thought it would be.

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:06.830
Yoshimoto-sama, the carp's ready.

00:10:08.180 --> 00:10:11.710
Just a little more! A little more!

00:10:12.330 --> 00:10:16.970
<i>There's no way Kotaro 
can do it and I can't!</i>

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:28.940
Yoshimoto-sama, let's head back.

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:33.020
Shut up! I'm not going back 
until I catch something!

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:39.650
Kotaro, what do I do?

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:41.320
Yoshimoto-sama!

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:44.830
Pull the rod so it doesn't get away!

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:46.440
Get away?

00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:47.830
What do you mean get away?

00:10:48.170 --> 00:10:51.320
Just pull the rod so it doesn't escape!

00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:53.860
I know that!

00:10:53.860 --> 00:10:56.400
But what do I do?

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:59.220
You just have to kind 
of have a feel for it!

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:02.680
That doesn't help me!

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:07.180
That's it, Yoshimoto-sama!

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:09.430
What's it?

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:14.520
Wow!

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:17.740
It's not that big.

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:24.350
I did it!

00:11:24.350 --> 00:11:27.290
This is the first carp that I, 
Imagawa Yoshimoto,

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:30.160
have ever fished!

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:47.350
I'll never forget this 
beautiful sunset.

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:21.630
<b>Lure Fishing 
for Beginners</b>

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:21.630
<b>Dace Fishing</b>

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:21.630
<b>Carp Fishing's 
Ultimate Manual</b>

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:25.140
<b>Salmon Season!</b>

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:28.140
<b>Zero Fishing: Tackle for Larger Fish</b>

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:03.960
What is it?

00:13:11.320 --> 00:13:14.240
<i>Zero Fishing, as the name implies,</i>

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:16.560
<i>is setting your tackle with 
almost nothing in weight.</i>

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:19.520
<i>A minuscule little hook.</i>

00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:22.280
<i>A thin, invisible line.</i>

00:13:24.040 --> 00:13:28.560
<i>It's so light that throwing 
it hard is impossible.</i>

00:13:30.770 --> 00:13:33.330
<i>But you don't need strength.</i>

00:13:35.090 --> 00:13:38.250
<i>You just need to entrust 
yourself to the flow.</i>

00:13:45.900 --> 00:13:51.680
The queen of the rapids 
is no match for me now.

00:13:52.240 --> 00:13:55.520
Which means I must...

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:14.600
This is what they call a hidden treasure!

00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:17.160
I'm glad I climbed this far.

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:27.590
This presence...

00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:57.400
That is the master of this swamp...

00:14:57.400 --> 00:15:00.750
How divine!

00:15:06.510 --> 00:15:09.900
<i>It's a carp, but at 
that size, it has plenty</i>

00:15:09.900 --> 00:15:12.360
<i>of experience and intelligence.</i>

00:15:13.230 --> 00:15:16.180
<i>Which means bread fishing 
is out of the question.</i>

00:15:29.130 --> 00:15:31.570
<b>Lure Fishing
for Beginners</b>

00:15:38.130 --> 00:15:40.490
I knew this wouldn't be good enough

00:15:40.490 --> 00:15:43.080
to trick the master of the swamp.

00:15:48.600 --> 00:15:51.550
<i>What the master of the
swamp doesn't know...</i>

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:56.130
<i>I need something no one's ever tried.</i>

00:15:59.170 --> 00:16:00.360
Kotaro!

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:02.350
What is it, Yoshimoto-sama?

00:16:02.820 --> 00:16:04.970
Go buy this for me.

00:16:04.970 --> 00:16:06.270
What is this?

00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:08.110
I'm counting on you.

00:16:08.130 --> 00:16:09.610
<b>Boilie Mix</b>

00:16:08.130 --> 00:16:09.610
<b>Imo-youkan</b>

00:16:14.810 --> 00:16:17.150
<i>If I make a boilie to 
bait the hook with,</i>

00:16:17.150 --> 00:16:19.830
<i>and add in something 
no one's ever used...</i>

00:16:20.390 --> 00:16:22.520
<i>I'll mix in imo-youkan!</i>

00:16:22.520 --> 00:16:25.830
<i>The master of the swamp should 
love delicious things!</i>

00:16:27.020 --> 00:16:29.170
<i>This is sure to work!</i>

00:16:34.420 --> 00:16:37.470
<i>I thought it would...</i>

00:16:58.880 --> 00:17:00.450
<i>Day five...</i>

00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:03.390
<i>Will it come out today?</i>

00:17:03.390 --> 00:17:09.590
<i>If I could at least see it...</i>

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:17.570
<i>I can't reel it in...</i>

00:17:17.570 --> 00:17:19.890
<i>It has to be the master of the swamp!</i>

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:31.070
<i>It got away...</i>

00:17:32.520 --> 00:17:35.070
<i>But why today?</i>

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:37.420
<i>The same bait.</i>

00:17:37.890 --> 00:17:39.280
<i>And the same spot...</i>

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:42.360
<i>What changed?</i>

00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:46.620
Me!

00:17:47.730 --> 00:17:51.130
It let its guard down 
because I was asleep!

00:17:51.820 --> 00:17:52.860
<i>In other words...</i>

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:56.470
I can't reel it in when all I
can think about is reeling it in!

00:18:01.360 --> 00:18:04.270
<i>They say your enemy can
sense your plot to kill them.</i>

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:06.550
<i>It's the same thing.</i>

00:18:06.550 --> 00:18:09.810
<i>My trying to fish it 
kept the master away.</i>

00:18:10.490 --> 00:18:14.900
<i>Which means, if I can eliminate 
my intent to fish it...</i>

00:18:16.020 --> 00:18:18.380
<i>The master will come!</i>

00:18:51.390 --> 00:18:54.780
Yoshimoto-sama, you'll catch a cold.

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:59.080
She doesn't see the rain now.

00:18:59.080 --> 00:19:00.510
She doesn't?

00:19:02.060 --> 00:19:03.480
Not just the rain.

00:19:04.190 --> 00:19:08.290
The only thing she sees now 
is the master of the swamp.

00:19:09.610 --> 00:19:13.790
At this point, all we can do is watch.

00:19:22.020 --> 00:19:24.390
<i>The time has come!</i>

00:20:12.240 --> 00:20:15.020
<i>Why didn't I realize before</i>

00:20:16.090 --> 00:20:20.350
<i>that the world is so simple?</i>

00:20:49.050 --> 00:20:53.580
This was what you were trying 
to teach me, wasn't it?

00:20:54.810 --> 00:20:55.890
Thank you.

00:20:58.370 --> 00:20:59.570
Yoshimoto-sama.

00:21:00.730 --> 00:21:02.400
The master got away,

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:05.160
but it seems you fished 
up something even better.

00:21:06.260 --> 00:21:10.160
My lack of conviction must have worried you, didn't it?

00:21:10.770 --> 00:21:14.920
No, I knew you would realize someday.

00:21:15.780 --> 00:21:19.670
So you knew everything, Sessai-sensei.

00:21:22.270 --> 00:21:23.420
Kotaro!

00:21:24.440 --> 00:21:25.220
Yes, ma'am.

00:21:25.790 --> 00:21:27.680
Fire an arrow to alert Sou'un.

00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:31.030
We will launch a full-scale 
attack on Nobunaga!

00:21:31.590 --> 00:21:32.240
Right!

00:21:40.660 --> 00:21:45.400
Nobunaga, I'll pay you 
back for all you've done.

00:21:54.040 --> 00:21:56.580
Looks like it's time.

00:21:58.120 --> 00:22:01.890
A revenge match against an 
opponent the lord lost to once!

00:22:01.890 --> 00:22:04.510
And I get to participate...

00:22:04.510 --> 00:22:06.550
I'm all fired up!

00:23:46.530 --> 00:23:49.080
The last episode could 
only be about me,

00:23:49.080 --> 00:23:51.300
the Little Devil King!

00:23:51.780 --> 00:23:55.200
Next time on Sengoku Collection: 
"Sengoku Collection!"

00:23:55.640 --> 00:23:58.200
I'll show how big a heroine can be!
